      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Fry the bacon in a dry pan over medium-high heat until crisp. Drain on kitchen paper."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Toast the bread. Spread mayonnaise generously on all four slices."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Season the tomato slices with salt and pepper. Layer the lettuce on two slices of toast, then the tomato, then the bacon. Top with the remaining toast. Press down gently and cut diagonally."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The details that matter"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Bacon must be crisp: not soft or chewy. Fry until it is beginning to look almost overdone. Tomato must be seasoned: unseasoned tomato in a sandwich tastes bland. Mayonnaise must cover the bread all the way to the edges. And eat immediately: a BLT that has sat for more than 10 minutes becomes soggy."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
